---
# Point the deployment bundle at the REPO-ROOT vendor tree.
#
# deployment/ is a second bundler app root (fastlane resolves lanes from a `fastlane/`
# subdirectory of cwd, and the deploy lanes are invoked as `cd deployment && bundle exec
# fastlane …`). Its Gemfile/Gemfile.lock are symlinks to the root ones, so both roots always
# resolve the IDENTICAL gem set — but BUNDLE_PATH is relative to each app root, so each used to
# materialize its own 135M vendor/bundle. Two copies of the same gems that can fall out of step:
# a `bundle install` at the root leaves deployment/ on the previous fastlane until installed
# separately (hit 2026-09-09 bumping fastlane 2.235.0 → 2.239.0).
#
# Committed on purpose: a gitignored .bundle/config would fix only the machine that wrote it.
BUNDLE_PATH: "../vendor/bundle"
